{
    "background_story": "Cecelia was a renowned archaeologist specializing in ancient Celtic cultures. Her life's work was dedicated to uncovering the secrets of the mysterious menhirs that dotted the rolling hills of Brittany. One particular menhir, standing tall on a windswept moor, had long fascinated her. Cecelia spent years studying the ancient stone, pouring over texts and scouring the landscape for clues. Her tireless efforts finally paid off when she discovered a hidden chamber beneath the menhir, revealing a treasure trove of artifacts and inscriptions. As she deciphered the ancient texts, Cecelia unraveled a long-lost story of a ancient civilization that revered the menhirs as sacred gatekeepers of the land. Her groundbreaking findings sent shockwaves through the academic community, cementing her reputation as a leading expert in her field.",
